{
  "$comment": [
    "The rich-text grammar contract shared by @comvi/core, @comvi/typegen (readMessage) and the platform's parser. js-sdk owns this file; the platform keeps a sha256-checked copy.",
    "message and render are a string, or {nest: {times, wrap, inner, before?, after?}}: s = inner; for i from times - 1 down to 0, with [open, close] = wrap[i % wrap.length], s = open + s + close; the string is before + s + after.",
    "render: the message rendered with `values` (or the record's own `values`) and, for every tag-like name in the message (`<` or `</` then a letter, then letters, digits, `_` or `-`), or only for the names in the record's `handlers`, a handler that returns `[name:` + its children joined + `]`. null when the message does not compile (it renders its key).",
    "schema: what the generated types ask for. params as readMessage reports them; tags lists CLOSED tags only, ordered by the opening of each name's first closed occurrence. null when the message does not compile.",
    "error: null, or `syntax` when the message does not compile. unclosed: the names of the never-closed opening tags, once per occurrence, in message order (each renders as its own text and gets one development warning); [] when the message does not compile.",
    "depthLimit: the height of the compiled tree a message may have. Each ICU sub-message level (a repeated selector's too) and each closed tag, self-closing included, adds one; a never-closed tag is text and adds nothing."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "depthLimit": 200,
  "values": {
    "n": 1,
    "name": "N"
  },
